wc3-server

This repository is open-source glue (docker-compose, configuration templates,
Dockerfiles, entrypoints, and docs) that composes third-party open-source
software. The glue is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). The software
it builds carries its own licenses:

- PvPGN-PRO (the Battle.net realm) is licensed under the GNU General Public
  License v2.0. This repo builds it from upstream source; it does not modify or
  redistribute PvPGN binaries.
- aura-bot (the autohost bot) is distributed under its own upstream license;
  this repo builds it from a pinned upstream commit.
- The wc3-relay tunnel daemon is built from the separate wc3-launcher repository
  (github.com/PjSalty/wc3-launcher) under its own license.

No Blizzard Entertainment software, binaries, or game data are distributed by
this repository. Warcraft III and Battle.net are trademarks of Blizzard
Entertainment, Inc. You must own Warcraft III and supply your own game data
(for example common.j and blizzard.j from your own installation) to enable map
hosting. The open-source W3L loader lets a classic client connect to a
non-Blizzard realm; the game client itself is never redistributed here.
